External knowledge that might be helpful: 
The assumptions include:
- consider only those series that have CT modality and do not belong to the NLST collection
- filter out DICOM images that use the following two compression formats:
    - JPEG Lossless, Non-Hierarchical, First-Order Prediction, 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70;
    - JPEG Baseline (Process 1), 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51;
- do not contain localizer image type
- all instances in a series have identical values for image orientation (patient) and pixel spacing (converted to string before comparison)
- all instances in a series have 1 ± 0.01 as the dot product between the two vectors below:
    - cross product of first and second vectors;
    - vector [0, 0, 1];
- have number of instances in the series equal to the number of distinct values of Image Position (Patient) attribute (converted to string for comparison)
- all instances in a series have identical values for the first two components of Image Position (Patient)
- all instances in a series have identical pixel rows, and similarly identical pixel columns
- for the difference between the values of the 3rd component of Image Position (Patient), after sorting all instances by that third component


BTW, the desired output report should contain:
1. The unique identifier for each image series;
2. The number assigned to the series within a study;
3. The unique identifier for the study that the series belongs to;
4. The unique identifier for the patient;
5. The maximum dot product value between the cross product of image orientation vectors and a reference vector, indicating geometric alignment;
6. The total number of SOP instances (individual images) in each series;
7. The number of distinct slice thickness values within the series;
8. The maximum and minimum difference between consecutive slice intervals (the z-coordinate spacing);
9. The tolerance value for slice interval differences (the z-coordinate spacing);
10. The number of distinct exposure values;
11. The maximum and minimum exposure value recorded for the images;
12. The difference between the maximum and minimum exposure values within the series, indicating the range of exposure variation;
13. The total size of the image series in megabytes (MiB).
And please sort the final output by slice interval difference tolerance, maximum exposure difference and series unique ID (all in descending order).
The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'IDC': {'IDC_V17': ['DICOM_ALL']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant column shortlist and how they may be used (only the columns that matter for the requested QC‑filters and final metrics)

• "Modality" : modality filter (keep CT only)  
• "collection_name" : exclude rows that belong to ‘NLST’  
• "TransferSyntaxUID" : eliminate JPEG–compressed images (UIDs 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70 and 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51)  
• "ImageType" : string that reveals “LOCALIZER” views – to be rejected  
• "SeriesInstanceUID" : unique identifier of a series (report field #1, grouping key)  
• "SeriesNumber" : number assigned to the series inside a study (report field #2)  
• "StudyInstanceUID" : unique identifier of the study (report field #3)  
• "PatientID" : submitter’s patient identifier (report field #4)  
• "ImageOrientationPatient" : six‑numbers array, needed to compute the cross‑product and dot‑product test (report field #5)  
• "PixelSpacing" : two‑numbers array, needs to be identical in the series  
• "ImagePositionPatient" : three‑numbers array – used for positional tests & slice interval statistics (report fields #8‑#9)  
• "Rows", "Columns" : pixel matrix size – must be constant inside the series  
• "SliceThickness" : used to count distinct thickness values (report field #7)  
• "Exposure" (plus other exposure‑like attributes such as "ExposureInmAs", "XRayTubeCurrentInmA") : used for exposure statistics (#10‑#12)  
• "instance_size" : byte size of each SOP instance – to derive total MiB of the series (#13)  
• "instance_size", "SOPInstanceUID" : for counting SOPs and estimating the aggregated size (#6, #13)

Below are ten exploratory / building‑block queries (simple → complex → near‑final) – each limited to 20 rows – that progressively check the content of the single table  
IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL.  All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes as required.

```sql
-- 1) Distinct collections that are present in the table
SELECT DISTINCT "collection_name"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Count how many rows per modality – helps to see how many CT rows exist
SELECT "Modality",
       COUNT(*)    AS "row_cnt"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
GROUP  BY "Modality"
ORDER  BY "row_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Transfer‑syntax UIDs that appear in CT data – to confirm which JPEG UIDs to exclude
SELECT DISTINCT "TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE  "Modality" = 'CT'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Quick look at any rows that seem to be localizers
SELECT "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "ImageType"
FROM   "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE  "ImageType" ILIKE '%LOCALIZER%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Sample the six orientation numbers and a quick dot‑product check for some series
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[0]::FLOAT AS "r1",
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[1]::FLOAT AS "r2",
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[3]::FLOAT AS "c1",
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[4]::FLOAT AS "c2",
        ABS( ("ImageOrientationPatient")[0]::FLOAT * ("ImageOrientationPatient")[4]::FLOAT
           - ("ImageOrientationPatient")[1]::FLOAT * ("ImageOrientationPatient")[3]::FLOAT )
        AS "dot_prod_z"
FROM    "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE   "Modality" = 'CT'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) How many SOP instances per series after the basic CT / NLST / JPEG / LOCALIZER filters
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        COUNT(*) AS "sop_cnt"
FROM    "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE   "Modality"         = 'CT'
  AND   "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
  AND   "TransferSyntaxUID" NOT IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70', '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51')
  AND  ( "ImageType" IS NULL OR NOT ("ImageType" ILIKE '%LOCALIZER%') )
GROUP  BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Check that each candidate series holds exactly one PixelSpacing value
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        COUNT(DISTINCT TO_VARCHAR("PixelSpacing")) AS "distinct_pix_spc"
FROM    "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE   "Modality"         = 'CT'
  AND   "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
GROUP  BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT TO_VARCHAR("PixelSpacing")) > 1      -- flag bad ones
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Compare number of SOPs with number of distinct Z positions (third component of ImagePositionPatient)
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        COUNT(*)                                  AS "sop_cnt",
        COUNT(DISTINCT TO_VARCHAR(("ImagePositionPatient")[2])) AS "distinct_z"
FROM    "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
WHERE   "Modality" = 'CT'
GROUP  BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
HAVING COUNT(*) <> COUNT(DISTINCT TO_VARCHAR(("ImagePositionPatient")[2]))
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Simple slice‑interval statistics for a handful of series (max / min Δz)
WITH base AS (
    SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
            ("ImagePositionPatient")[2]::FLOAT AS "z_coord"
    FROM    "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
    WHERE   "Modality" = 'CT'
)
, diffs AS (
    SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
            ABS("z_coord" - LAG("z_coord") OVER (PARTITION BY "SeriesInstanceUID" ORDER BY "z_coord")) AS "z_diff"
    FROM    base
)
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        MAX("z_diff") AS "max_z_diff",
        MIN("z_diff") AS "min_z_diff"
FROM    diffs
GROUP  BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Near‑final query – gathers all requested metrics, applies geometry & QC filters, and sorts by tolerance / exposure range / UID
WITH filtered AS (   -- basic content filter
    SELECT
        "SeriesInstanceUID",
        "SeriesNumber",
        "StudyInstanceUID",
        "PatientID",
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[0]::FLOAT AS r1,
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[1]::FLOAT AS r2,
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[2]::FLOAT AS r3,
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[3]::FLOAT AS c1,
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[4]::FLOAT AS c2,
        ("ImageOrientationPatient")[5]::FLOAT AS c3,
        TO_VARCHAR("PixelSpacing")                 AS pix_spc_str,
        ("ImagePositionPatient")[0]::FLOAT         AS pos_x,
        ("ImagePositionPatient")[1]::FLOAT         AS pos_y,
        ("ImagePositionPatient")[2]::FLOAT         AS pos_z,
        TRY_TO_FLOAT("SliceThickness")             AS slice_thk,
        TRY_TO_FLOAT("Exposure")                   AS exposure_val,
        "Rows"                                     AS rows_val,
        "Columns"                                  AS cols_val,
        "instance_size"
    FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_ALL"
    WHERE "Modality" = 'CT'
      AND "collection_name" <> 'NLST'
      AND "TransferSyntaxUID" NOT IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70','1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51')
      AND ( "ImageType" IS NULL OR NOT ("ImageType" ILIKE '%LOCALIZER%') )
)
, per_series AS (    -- tests that everything is internally consistent
    SELECT
        "SeriesInstanceUID",
        MAX("SeriesNumber")      AS "SeriesNumber",
        MAX("StudyInstanceUID")  AS "StudyInstanceUID",
        MAX("PatientID")         AS "PatientID",
        ABS( MIN(r1)*MIN(c2) - MIN(r2)*MIN(c1) )  AS dot_prod,
        COUNT(*)                 AS sop_cnt,
        COUNT(DISTINCT TO_VARCHAR(pos_z))         AS distinct_z,
        COUNT(DISTINCT pix_spc_str)               AS distinct_pix_spc,
        COUNT(DISTINCT rows_val)                  AS distinct_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT cols_val)                  AS distinct_cols,
        COUNT(DISTINCT slice_thk)                 AS distinct_thk,
        SUM("instance_size")/(1024*1024)          AS series_mib
    FROM   filtered
    GROUP  BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
    HAVING
          dot_prod BETWEEN 0.99 AND 1.01                    -- geometric alignment
      AND distinct_pix_spc = 1                              -- unique pixel spacing
      AND sop_cnt = distinct_z                              -- SOP count equals slice count
      AND distinct_rows = 1 AND distinct_cols = 1           -- constant matrix size
)
, z_diffs AS (
    SELECT  f."SeriesInstanceUID",
            ABS(pos_z - LAG(pos_z) OVER (PARTITION BY f."SeriesInstanceUID" ORDER BY pos_z)) AS z_diff
    FROM    filtered f
    JOIN    per_series p
      ON    p."SeriesInstanceUID" = f."SeriesInstanceUID"
)
, z_stats AS (
    SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
            MAX(z_diff)                       AS max_z_diff,
            MIN(z_diff)                       AS min_z_diff,
            MAX(z_diff) - MIN(z_diff)         AS tol_z_diff
    FROM    z_diffs
    GROUP  BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
)
, exp_stats AS (
    SELECT  f."SeriesInstanceUID",
            COUNT(DISTINCT exposure_val)      AS num_exp_vals,
            MAX(exposure_val)                 AS max_exposure,
            MIN(exposure_val)                 AS min_exposure,
            MAX(exposure_val) - MIN(exposure_val) AS diff_exposure
    FROM    filtered f
    JOIN    per_series p
      ON    p."SeriesInstanceUID" = f."SeriesInstanceUID"
    GROUP  BY f."SeriesInstanceUID"
)
SELECT
    p."SeriesInstanceUID"                                                AS "series_uid",      -- #1
    p."SeriesNumber"                                                     AS "series_number",   -- #2
    p."StudyInstanceUID"                                                 AS "study_uid",       -- #3
    p."PatientID"                                                        AS "patient_id",      -- #4
    p.dot_prod                                                           AS "max_dot",         -- #5
    p.sop_cnt                                                            AS "num_sop",         -- #6
    p.distinct_thk                                                       AS "num_slice_thk",   -- #7
    z.max_z_diff                                                         AS "max_delta_z",     -- #8
    z.min_z_diff                                                         AS "min_delta_z",     -- #8
    z.tol_z_diff                                                         AS "delta_z_tol",     -- #9
    e.num_exp_vals                                                       AS "num_exposure_vals",--#10
    e.max_exposure                                                       AS "max_exposure",    -- #11
    e.min_exposure                                                       AS "min_exposure",    -- #11
    e.diff_exposure                                                      AS "exposure_range",  -- #12
    p.series_mib                                                         AS "series_mib"       -- #13
FROM   per_series  p
JOIN   z_stats     z  ON z."SeriesInstanceUID" = p."SeriesInstanceUID"
JOIN   exp_stats   e  ON e."SeriesInstanceUID" = p."SeriesInstanceUID"
ORDER  BY z.tol_z_diff  DESC NULLS LAST,
          e.diff_exposure DESC NULLS LAST,
          p."SeriesInstanceUID" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

